{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker(store:)"},{"text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"text":". A segment is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore()"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps every event type declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" in the program’s modules, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore(events:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps only the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" types it lists. Each record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":", part of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":") writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" writes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" property, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"date in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date]"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date?]"},{"type":"text","text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type of your own or in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types, such as one that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run but never written, and reported once as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drop is reported on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the oldest segments"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set. Call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", after the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":", as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"GRDBPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Persistence","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Persistence"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Stores","anchor":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A store keeping events of the types "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directory"},{"type":"text","text":"; it recovers the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already there."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"events"},{"kind":"text","text":": [any ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Event","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Codable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7Codablea"},{"kind":"text","text":").Type], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"directory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FilePath","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"byteBound"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"segmentByteCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SegmentStoreError","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence17SegmentStoreErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/init(events:directory:bytebound:segmentbytecount:)","title":"init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/persistingrecords":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persisting Records"}],"title":"Persisting Records","type":"link","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","kind":"symbol","title":"DropReport","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":"), so it survives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"synchronize"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","title":"synchronize()"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStoreError":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SegmentStoreError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" throws: an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"argument it can’t open a store with, or the file system’s failure."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStoreError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstoreerror","type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","kind":"symbol","title":"RecordStore","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"title":"dropReports","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"title":"Persistence","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/changingevents":{"title":"Changing Events","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Changing Events","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/notPersisted(event:)":{"title":"DropReport.notPersisted(event:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/notpersisted(event:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"notPersisted"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","abstract":[{"text":"A record of the event named ","type":"text"},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was kept in memory only because its type isn’t one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": its records are delivered in this run, but never written, so they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lost if the app ends first. Reported once per type, on its first record, for as long as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store lives; a type left out by mistake is added to ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}}}